  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q01", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "mcq", "difficulty": 1,
   "stem": {"en": "Which fraction is equivalent to 1/2?", "te": "1/2 కి సమాన భిన్నం ఏది?"},
   "options": [
     {"id": "a", "text": {"en": "2/3", "te": "2/3"}, "isCorrect": false, "misconceptionCode": "F-EQUIV-ADD"},
     {"id": "b", "text": {"en": "3/6", "te": "3/6"}, "isCorrect": true},
     {"id": "c", "text": {"en": "1/4", "te": "1/4"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "d", "text": {"en": "2/1", "te": "2/1"}, "isCorrect": false}],
   "solution": {"en": "Multiply top and bottom of 1/2 by 3: 3/6.", "te": "1/2 లో లవ హారాలను 3 తో గుణించు: 3/6."},
   "boardTags": ["NCERT", "TS_SCERT"], "reviewStatus": "draft"},
  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q02", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "numeric", "difficulty": 1,
   "stem": {"en": "Fill in the blank: 2/5 = ?/10", "te": "ఖాళీ నింపు: 2/5 = ?/10"},
   "answer": 4,
   "wrongAnswers": [{"value": 7, "misconceptionCode": "F-EQUIV-ADD"}],
   "solution": {"en": "5 × 2 = 10, so multiply the top by 2 as well: 2 × 2 = 4.", "te": "5 × 2 = 10, కాబట్టి లవాన్నీ 2 తో గుణించు: 2 × 2 = 4."},
   "boardTags": ["NCERT", "TS_SCERT"], "tags": ["paper_friendly"], "reviewStatus": "draft"},
  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q03", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "mcq", "difficulty": 2,
   "stem": {"en": "Which fraction is NOT equivalent to 2/3?", "te": "ఏ భిన్నం 2/3 కి సమానం కాదు?"},
   "options": [
     {"id": "a", "text": {"en": "4/6", "te": "4/6"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "b", "text": {"en": "10/15", "te": "10/15"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "c", "text": {"en": "3/4", "te": "3/4"}, "isCorrect": true},
     {"id": "d", "text": {"en": "6/9", "te": "6/9"}, "isCorrect": false}],
   "solution": {"en": "4/6, 6/9 and 10/15 all come from multiplying 2/3; 3/4 comes from adding 1, which does not keep the value.", "te": "4/6, 6/9, 10/15 అన్నీ 2/3 ను గుణించడం ద్వారా వస్తాయి; 3/4, 1 కలపడం ద్వారా వస్తుంది, అది విలువను నిలపదు."},
   "boardTags": ["NCERT", "TS_SCERT"], "reviewStatus": "draft"},
  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q04", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "mcq", "difficulty": 2,
   "stem": {"en": "What is 18/24 in its simplest form?", "te": "18/24 యొక్క కనిష్ఠ రూపం ఏది?"},
   "options": [
     {"id": "a", "text": {"en": "9/12", "te": "9/12"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "b", "text": {"en": "6/8", "te": "6/8"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "c", "text": {"en": "2/3", "te": "2/3"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "d", "text": {"en": "3/4", "te": "3/4"}, "isCorrect": true}],
   "solution": {"en": "The HCF of 18 and 24 is 6: 18 ÷ 6 = 3 and 24 ÷ 6 = 4, so 3/4.", "te": "18, 24 ల గ.సా.భా. 6: 18 ÷ 6 = 3, 24 ÷ 6 = 4, కాబట్టి 3/4."},
   "boardTags": ["NCERT", "TS_SCERT"], "reviewStatus": "draft"},
  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q05", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "mcq", "difficulty": 3,
   "stem": {"en": "Write 3/5 as an equivalent fraction with denominator 10.", "te": "3/5 ను హారం 10 ఉన్న సమాన భిన్నంగా రాయి."},
   "options": [
     {"id": "a", "text": {"en": "8/10", "te": "8/10"}, "isCorrect": false, "misconceptionCode": "F-EQUIV-ADD"},
     {"id": "b", "text": {"en": "6/10", "te": "6/10"}, "isCorrect": true},
     {"id": "c", "text": {"en": "3/10", "te": "3/10"}, "isCorrect": false},
     {"id": "d", "text": {"en": "5/10", "te": "5/10"}, "isCorrect": false}],
   "solution": {"en": "5 × 2 = 10, so 3 × 2 = 6: 6/10. Adding 5 to the top (8/10) changes the value.", "te": "5 × 2 = 10, కాబట్టి 3 × 2 = 6: 6/10. లవానికి 5 కలిపితే (8/10) విలువ మారుతుంది."},
   "boardTags": ["NCERT", "TS_SCERT"], "reviewStatus": "draft"},
  {"id": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV.Q06", "conceptId": "M6.FRAC.EQUIV", "type": "numeric", "difficulty": 3,
